On Sat, Dec 12, 2015 at 12:02 AM, Rui Liu <edenish.fallen@gmail.com> wrote:

>  A list of a thousand cmavo for merely grammatical use seems that the
> language focuses too much on grammar.
>

Most cmavo carry semantic content. The grammatical structure classes
(selma'o) are something like a hundred, but some selma'o (UI, BAI, PA, ...)
have a lot of differnet cmavo with semantic content.


> (Maybe it's the cost of syntax unambiguity?)
>

Nah, it's mostly bells and whistles. The core syntax can do with even fewer
selma'o.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

